cking apples  again some tyrannical European guy sails  to the Americas and brutalizes the  natives you've made 6.2 billion dollars  and worked for fifteen hundred and four  years a bunch of guys in white wigs  decide Britain sucks and sign a piece of  paper you've made seven point nine  billion dollars and worked for seventeen  hundred and eighty years everyone is  scared that a 1 turning into a 2 will  break the world you've made eight point  three billion dollars and worked for two  thousand and three years one day after  over 2,000 years of working in your  little orchard you realize it's getting  difficult to pick apples again your back  hurts your eyes are blurry and the Apple  seemed so far away you decide to stop  and count your money again the year is  2020 you've made eight point four  billion dollars and you've worked for  2020 for years two thousand dollars per  hour forty hours per week  fifty-two  weeks per year for 2024 years you smile  to yourself eight point four billion  dollars surely after working all those  years you are now the richest person on  earth you take some of your money and  buy yourself a smartphone time to look  up the list of the wealthiest people  alive to your shock you're not at the  top of the list in fact you're not even  close there are 57 names above you in  the United States alone  hopefully this thought experiment has  helped put into perspective just how  staggeringly huge numbers in the  billions are our stick figure friend  worked for over 2,000 years and still  didn't crack the top 50 wealthiest  people in America list and that's at  $2,000 per hour think how many people  don't make that in a month there's  another version of this experiment that  starts at Christopher Columbus's first  voyage and assumes five thousand dollars  per day by 2020 you wouldn't even have  made 1 billion dollars five hundred  twenty eight years at five thousand  dollars a day and you still wouldn't be  a billionaire now try it with your  income here's the formula take your  hourly wage x forty four full-time fifty  to four weeks in the year and then try  different numbers for the years required  for example if you make ten dollars an  hour it would take you over forty eight  thousand years to make a billion dollars  so what's the takeaway here if you ask  me it's that how we value contributions  to society is deeply flawed look at Jeff  Bezos as of writing the script he's  worth a hundred and twenty three billion  dollars for what realizing that you can  sell books online no one earns that kind  of money frankly it's obscene meanwhile  people who perform critical roles like  teaching are paid peanuts and on top of  that are expected to buy their own  classroom supplies if the market decides  what's valuable and comes to the  conclusion that people who destroy small  businesses and exploit their workers are  what's truly worthy of billions of  dollars maybe the market as it exists  needs to go to finish off our thought  experiment let's do one more calculation  in order for our stick figure to make a  hundred and twenty three billion dollars  he would have to work full-time at two  thousand dollars per hour with no  vacations and saving every penny for  twenty nine thousand six hundred years  Bezos started Amazon when he was thirty  years old he's now 56 no one earns a  billion dollars and it is shameful that  anyone could ever be  worth a hundred and twenty three billion  dollars don't get me wrong Bezos is a  smart guy but no one is worth a hundred  twenty three billion dollars the system  needs to change if you enjoyed this  video and would like to see more like it  consider subscribing to stay up to date  with my latest episodes if you hated it  feel free to drop a thumbs down and tell  me why I'm stupid in the comments if you  really want to help support my channel I  just started a patreon which you can  find at patreon.com slash second thought  you can check out some of my previous  work by click